        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- PAPER 6 -->
      <div class="pub-item" data-category="monte-carlo">
        <div class="pub-year">1989</div>
        <div class="pub-body">
          <p class="pub-title">Free Energies in Solution from Monte Carlo Simulations</p>
          <p class="pub-authors">W. L. Jorgensen</p>
          <p class="pub-journal">Accounts of Chemical Research · 1989 · Vol. 22, p. 184</p>
          <p class="pub-desc">A foundational review of Monte Carlo methodology for computing free energies of solvation, conformational equilibria, and chemical reactions in solution. Surveys the statistical perturbation theory framework implemented in BOSS and demonstrates its application to a range of chemical systems. Established the conceptual and practical basis for free energy calculations in solution that underpins all of the Foundation's simulation programs.</p>
          <div class="pub-tags">
            <span class="pub-tag">Monte Carlo</span>
            <span class="pub-tag">Free Energy</span>
            <span class="pub-tag">BOSS</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pub-actions">
